 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Glared gleam from the lurid sky\nOn flood of feverly light,\nA power that spoke alone\nEven as the words of death, again\nAnd as the words of heaven. Again\nOut of its darkened dome in heaven\nIt gave its gracious command again;\nAgain it met our voices,\nLighter and warmer being\nThan the darkness but than fire,\nThrough the burning room of night to heaven,\nIn the twilight's low day-light pouring down",
